.Dd August 27, 2026
.Dt C4IF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm c4if
.Nd utility to check exposed interfaces of C4 sources
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ah
.Op Fl I Ar dir | Fl I Cm -
.Op Fl v Ar vis
.Ar source
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads an roughly parses the top-level expressions within a given C4
source file and outputs C4 code in form of a list of function declarations that
show the interface provided by the original file.

The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Process
.Ar source
as a C4 archive instead of a source file.
.It Fl h
Print help information and exit 100.
.It Fl I Ar dir
Add
.Ar dir
as a search path when resolving libraries. If the special value
.Cm -
is used, the search path is cleared instead. This removes system paths as well.
.It Fl v Ar vis
Instead of public and internal visibility, print only functions that have a
visibility of
.Ar vis
or higher. The value can be any one of the following:
.Cm ~ Ns , or
.Cm internal
for the default internal or higher visibility;
.Cm + Ns , or
.Cm public
for only public functions or
.Cm - Ns ,
.Cm private Ns , or
.Cm all
for listing all functions. English word values can be passed by unique prefix.
.El
The output of this program is always valid and parsable as C4. Therefore, it
could be used to create files with
.Qq embedded dependencies
in them. That is, by replacing every
.Cm use
line with the output of
.Xr c4if 1
the file will become self-contained
.Em with respect to compilation .
That is, this will still require linking every dependency, unless you merge the
object files with some utility. Expect more tools to ease generating source
amalgamations in the future.

.Sh EXIT STATUS
On success,
.Nm
exits 0. In case of failure, the following are used:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 1
Invalid input format \(en either unparsable C4 source or malformed archive.
.It 100
Invalid invocation. Flags or arguments malformed or missing.
.It 101
Unexpected error. Please file a bug report.
.It 111
General runtime error: syscall failure or LLVM error.
.El
